# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository itself, regardless of
# a contributor's local core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows
# checkout re-introduces CRLF into working-tree copies of files that are
# supposed to be byte-identical to a plugin's own .zip/backend/plugins-bundled
# copy (see scripts/sync-plugins.mjs) - invisible locally (both sides end up
# CRLF, so they still "agree" with each other), but a real mismatch against
# what CI, and every real installer, actually checks out. Confirmed the hard
# way, more than once.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files genuinely want CRLF - leave this one alone rather
# than force it to LF along with everything else above.
run-dev.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary - never line-ending-normalize or diff these.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.zip binary
